# Session role privacy and media

Canonical: technical guide §11–§12 and video guide (LiveKit).

## Role privacy

- Server-authoritative: examiner-only content must never reach the candidate browser
- Filter in API/RSC payloads — CSS/UI hiding alone does **not** pass
- Candidate HTML, JSON, prefetch, logs, and analytics must exclude examiner guidance, follow-ups, rubric anchors, and future task answers
- After role switch, previous examiner content must not remain authorized on the old client
- Use LiveKit for media transport only; Flownic owns roles, timers, stages, completion

## Media

- Prefer LiveKit Cloud React prefabs (`PreJoin`, conference); avoid custom WebRTC
- Short-lived, room-scoped, server-issued tokens after auth + membership + join-window checks
- Opaque room names; never user names/emails
- Verify webhooks; make handlers idempotent
- Recording off by default; explicit consent if enabled
- Use the `livekit-agents` skill for LiveKit agent/realtime work

## Resilience

- Peer call survives AI/transcription failure
- Provider room end ≠ session complete
- Timer UI derives from server timestamps; do not write DB every second
